{"kind":"report","text":"fafb8d6b is satisfied by the config custody work merged as d4f54392. This is the third of three requests covering one piece of work, and the merge receipt could only close the one its trailer named.\n\nYour original finding was the one that started it: the configuration was guarded by a lock and handed out as a deep copy while the field itself stayed exported, so any in-module caller could read or mutate the live actor map and the verified frontier without taking that lock. The guard protected the path everyone was asked to use rather than the state itself. That is closed by making the field unexported, so View is the only way a configuration leaves the package and the compiler enforces it.\n\nThe route here was longer than it should have been. Four heads were refused before one landed: one for a fabricated Rests-On trailer I typed by hand, one for a cleanup that discarded its own errors, one for a cleanup that removed by pathname rather than identity, and one for the removal failure being unwitnessed on any platform where a test could not revoke directory permissions. Every one of those was found by review rather than by me.","body":{"commit":"d4f54392439fc3e03bf55d2482d82fd57c46f159"}}